 "text": "But between the attack on Wolmi-do and the main landing, the ebb tide left a gap of nearly twelve hours. Wolmi-do would be taken on the morning tide, and the main force would land only on the evening tide. That was more than enough time for the enemy to guess exactly where the main landing would come, and to rush in reinforcements.",
